            <ArticleTitle>Epidural blood patch with allogeneic blood for post-dural puncture headache.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>261-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A parturient suffered post dural puncture headache following accidental dural puncture during attempted epidural anesthesia for cesarean section. Post partum fever was regarded as a contraindication to autologous epidural blood patch; compatible and infection-free allogeneic blood was therefore used with good effect and without apparent complications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
